# v2 render pipeline (do not regress)

When editing `js/v2/Orchestrator.js` (class **SacredOrchestrator**, globals **`window.anuOrchestrator`** canonical / **`window.Orchestrator`** legacy alias), `js/v2/constants.js`, `js/v2/Trees.js`, `js/v2/V2Panel.js`, or boot order in `index.v2.html`:

**Before changing PiP WebGL behavior:** read `.cursor/rules/sacred-pip-map-protect.mdc` — parent `#pipCanvas` is the live map unless the user explicitly authorizes a different render path.

1. **PiP is a second full-scene WebGL pass** — `_renderPip()` renders `this.scene` again into `#pipCanvas`. That duplicates most world GPU cost; it is **not** included in the main HUD `renderer.info` triangle line.

2. **`V2_PIP_RENDER_EVERY_N_FRAMES`** (`constants.js`) — `0` disables PiP 3D, `1` is maximum GPU (every frame), `2` is the usual compromise. Policy logic: **`anu/RenderingGovernor.js`** (`shouldRenderPipSceneThisFrame`).

3. **HUD stats = main canvas only** — do not tell anyone “triangles dropped” based on HUD alone if PiP or guide overlays are on.

4. **Trees** — instanced `tree.glb` × `TREE_TARGET` usually dominates triangle counts before avatar/UI.

5. **Legacy ThreeIcons** — never assign onto `import * as THREE` namespace; use Proxy/pattern in `V2Panel.js`.

6. **Anu bridge** — rendering cadence: `anu/RenderingGovernor.js` + **`AdaptiveRenderPolicy`** (stress → wider PiP stride); typed interactions: `anu/InteractionBus.js` + `anu/anuEvents.js`. Errors + stress samples: **`anu/AnuErrorAndStressLedger.js`** (`AnuUniverse.exportStressJson()` / `exportAiStressBrief()`).

Runtime **memory + warnings**: `js/v2/AnuModule.js` (`window.AnuUniverse.report()`). Extend `ANU_PIPELINE_MEMORY` when a new incident is understood. **Scene drawables**: `anu/SceneModelInventory.js` (interval traverse; `summary.bySimulationDomain`). **Simulation overview**: `anu/SimulationController.js` (`AnuUniverse.exportSimulationJson()`).
